{"id": 22468, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 65-year-old woman is evaluated for worsening dyspnea.\u00a0 Medical history is significant for triple-negative breast cancer (negative for estrogen and progesterone receptors and HER2 amplification), which was treated with mastectomy followed by doxorubicin-based chemotherapy 2 years ago.\u00a0 Temperature is 37.2 C (99 F), blood pressure is 126/78 mm Hg, pulse is 94/min, and respirations are 18/min.\u00a0 Physical examination shows bilateral lung crackles.\u00a0 There is trace lower extremity edema.\u00a0 Chest x-ray reveals diffuse interstitial prominence, scattered fluffy opacities, and small bilateral pleural effusions.\u00a0 Which of the following most likely contributed to this patient's current symptoms?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Cross-signaling with T-cell antigen receptor"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Impaired tubulin heterodimer formation"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Inhibited oxidative phosphorylation"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Production of reactive oxygen species"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Reduced vascular endothelial growth factor signaling"}], "correctAnswer": "D", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_T38636\" style=\"overflow-x: auto; font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">T</mark>oxicities of common chemotherapeutic agents</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Chemotherapy agent</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Mechanism of action</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Toxicity</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Anthracyclines*</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">(eg, doxorubicin)</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Binds with topoisomerase II to cleave DNA</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Binds with iron to generate free radicals</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Dilated cardiomyopathy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Bleomycin</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Induces free radical formation</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Pulmonary fibrosis</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Cisplatin*</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Cross-links DNA to inhibit DNA synthesis</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nephrotoxicity</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Ototoxicity</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Peripheral neuropathy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Cyclophosphamide*</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Cross-links DNA to inhibit DNA synthesis</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Hemorrhagic cystitis</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Bladder cancer</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Paclitaxel</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Inhibits microtubule disassembly</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Neuropathy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Vincristine/</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">vinblastine</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Binds \u03b2-tubulin to inhibit microtubule formation</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Neuropathy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">*Drugs that induce DNA damage also increase risk for secondary malignancy.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This patient underwent doxorubicin-based chemotherapy 2 years ago and now has signs and symptoms of <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">heart failure</strong> (eg, progressive dyspnea, lower extremity edema, lung crackles with radiologic evidence of pulmonary edema and pleural effusion), indicating likely <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">anthracycline cardiotoxicity</strong>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Anthracyclines (eg, <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">doxorubicin</strong>, idarubicin, epirubicin, daunorubicin) are a class of chemotherapy agents used in a wide variety of cancers.\u00a0 However, they frequently cause <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">dose-dependent cardiotoxicity</strong> that impairs cardiac contractility.\u00a0 Although many patients who develop cardiotoxicity demonstrate no overt signs of heart failure and recover completely, a minority develop progressive cardiac impairment and <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">dilated cardiomyopathy</strong> within months or up to <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">several years after exposure</strong>, as in this patient.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Anthracyclines are thought to damage cardiomyocytes through the following major mechanisms:</p><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start inline\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Free radical production:</strong>\u00a0 Oxidation of anthracyclines generates free radicals that cause lipid peroxidation of cardiomyocyte membranes, vacuolization, and replacement with fibrous tissue.</p></li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Topoisomerase II\u2013mediated cell death:</strong>\u00a0 Topoisomerases cut DNA strands to alleviate DNA tangles and supercoils during transcription and replication.\u00a0 Doxorubicin binds to topoisomerase II and prevents it from releasing cut DNA strands, resulting in DNA breaks that halt proliferation of rapidly dividing cells (eg, cancer cells) and can result in apoptosis of healthy cells (eg, cardiomyocytes).</li></ul><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Patients who require treatment with anthracyclines typically undergo cardiac evaluation (eg, ECG, echocardiography) prior to therapy.\u00a0 Those with baseline impairments in cardiac function may require an alternate agent (or close monitoring) to reduce the risk for further cardiac damage.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice A)</strong>\u00a0 Immune checkpoint inhibitors (eg, ipilimumab, nivolumab) are cancer therapies that can induce cross-signaling with T-cell antigen receptors and facilitate immune-mediated lung damage (ie, pneumonitis).</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 Vinca alkaloids (eg, vincristine, vinblastine) are common chemotherapy drugs that impair tubulin heterodimers to prevent microtubular formation.\u00a0 Peripheral neuropathy is a common adverse effect.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice C)</strong>\u00a0 Inhibition of oxidative phosphorylation is a potential target of cancer therapy, but toxicity to healthy cells is a limiting factor.\u00a0 Cyanide, a highly toxic compound, binds to complex IV of the electron-transport chain to halt cellular oxidative phosphorylation.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice E)</strong>\u00a0 Vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) inhibitors (eg, bevacizumab, sorafenib) are used in cancer management and are associated with increased risk for bleeding and thrombotic complications.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Cardiotoxicity leading to dilated cardiomyopathy is a known adverse effect of anthracycline chemotherapy (eg, doxorubicin).\u00a0 This cardiotoxicity is likely due to free radical\u2013mediated cellular damage and topoisomerase II\u2013induced cellular apoptosis.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Cardiotoxicity leading to dilated cardiomyopathy is a known adverse effect of anthracycline chemotherapy (eg, doxorubicin).  This cardiotoxicity is likely due to free radical\u2013mediated cellular damage and topoisomerase II\u2013induced cellular apoptosis.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\